{"call_id":"call_q4AHS7ZRN7aXVsxIY7ZuYCqR","process_id":"4670","turn_id":"019ca7d5-7f41-7352-89bf-011b662ed0f0","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ1F --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ1F --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": \"01KJKWXHKKHZMP574E78F7BHA3\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:21:35.378Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:28:13.436Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKXGPK47G78073ZAWTM0P1Z\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:21:39.940Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution scope: sync triage filter state (status/tag/action) with URL query params, preserve state on refresh/back-forward, and add/update E2E coverage in triage.spec.ts for URL persistence behavior.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKXW7Y8BEV4QFNCM45EZHWR\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:27:58.153Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented URL-synced triage filters in packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte: status/action/tag now round-trip via query params using goto() and URL parsing, with filter state restored from URL on load and history navigation. Added AC-7 E2E coverage in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/triage.spec.ts for URL updates + restore/back-forward behavior. Verification: npm run build -w packages/web-ui; npx playwright test tests/e2e/triage.spec.ts -g \\\"filter selections update URL query params|restores filter selections from URL and supports back-forward history|action filter narrows cards by triage action and resets card index\\\" --workers=1 (3 passed). kspec validate still reports pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment issues unrelated to this task.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKXYE0D30BTM6EFR8XTGNW5\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:29:09.901Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #620: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/620 (branch feat/triage-url-filter-state, commit 8bd9485bb). Implemented triage URL query sync for status/action/tag filters with restore-on-load/history behavior and added AC-7 E2E coverage for URL update + back/forward restoration. Verification: npm run build -w packages/web-ui; targeted triage Playwright URL/filter tests passed (3/3); kspec validate reports pre-existing project-wide issues unrelated to this change.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": \"01KJKWXHKKHZMP574E78F7BHA3\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:21:35.378Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:28:13.436Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKXGPK47G78073Z